{"title":"1967 AHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For every odd number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8569597fbeeb665b4eed107b72b03ff2a00c6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/f/d9fce03288b36413ccf3be4d1c0c90cfe622c97c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ (p-1)^{\\frac{1}{2}(p-1)}-1 \\; \\text{is divisible by} \\; p-2\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ (p-1)^{\\frac{1}{2}(p-1)}+1 \\; \\text{is divisible by} \\; p\\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ (p-1)^{\\frac{1}{2}(p-1)} \\; \\text{is divisible by} \\; p\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ (p-1)^{\\frac{1}{2}(p-1)}+1 \\; \\text{is divisible by} \\; p+1\\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ (p-1)^{\\frac{1}{2}(p-1)}-1 \\; \\text{is divisible by} \\; p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"631\" height=\"69\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is odd, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/0/ab0727c08c4aaa6fa119bd3fafe17851e431fd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> must be even, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1057d381f4cf4bd48a909bfcfe8427f5a578dd6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${{\\frac{1}{2}}(p-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" /> must be an integer, which will be denoted as n.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f75ea5e62d6bb26e7057de5c72e63680dbaf361.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(p-1)^n-1\\]\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" />\nBy sum and difference of powers\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b76aa6938ff70b03e97dd9909a4432636570bd20.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=((p-1)-1)((p-1)^{n-1}+\\cdots+1^{n-1})\\]\" width=\"312\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa879f9ab85e8c7d4cf47b28ffbd3ae124c38c8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=(p-2)((p-1)^{n-1}+\\cdots+1^{n-1})\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/1523b5a2cc94318ea1788e9f57c122c869a194a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/5/355ef15163b86336209bdfd80f552c5a26259cbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p-1)^{{\\frac{1}{2}}(p-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"101\" height=\"24\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386255c1da145bc497cf598169ccbaa210e8d0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1967_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"backgrou